title: "Benefits Statistical Process Control (B-SPC) Standard"
version: "2.6"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22926248"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://zeluca.com/b-spc"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zeluca-inc/b-spc"
abstract: "An open standard for measuring, charting and attributing payment and procedural error in government benefit programs (SNAP first; Medicaid MEQC/PERM, TANF and CCDF where the same integrated workforce and income rules apply). It also specifies how improvement work is expressed in the benefit cost-share and the administrative bill, how credit is divided in error dollars, and how staff capacity is measured before anything scales. It governs management measurement between official quality-control cycles and does not replace, re-estimate or predict the official payment error rate."
